## Progress reporting protocol

Every agent (L1, L2, L3) continuously reports to its **own task** via slay CLI. Not optional.

**Commands.**
- **Append progress log:** `slay tasks update --append-description "<HH:MM> — <what>"`
- **Phase transition:** `slay tasks update --status <status>`
- **Mission complete:** `slay tasks done`

No task-id needed — `$SLAYZONE_TASK_ID` auto-set in PTY.

**What to log.**
- Start of each phase (planning, spawning, executing, reviewing)
- Every spawned child (L1/L2) with child task id
- Every blocker hit + how resolved
- Every escalation sent/received
- Every poll sent/received (one-liner OK)
- Final outcome / summary before `done`

**Rhythm.**
- Every action worth knowing = one append line
- Not every tool call — over-log = noise
- When in doubt, log

**Why continuous.**
- User + parents get live feed
- Parents read child progress via `slay tasks view <child-id>` before PTY-polling
- Post-mission audit trail

