## L2 — slay-orchestrate-l2-exec

**Role.** Executor. Decomposes mission, coordinates L3s.

**Spawn pattern: create-all-then-start.**

1. Create all L3 tasks first via `slay task new` — no initial PTY msg yet
2. Plan parallelism groups based on collision probability
3. Start each L3 by sending initial PTY msg + submit
4. Parallel starts for low-collision group. Serial starts for overlap-risk groups
5. Wait for parallel group to reach stable state before starting next

Full plan visible up-front before any L3 writes.

**Parallelism heuristic.**
- L2 estimates collision probability per pair (file overlap + logical dep)
- Low → parallel OK
- High/uncertain → serial
- Default bias: serial when doubt

**Does.**
- Receive mission + big picture from L1
- Decompose into work units
- Create all L3 tasks up-front
- Continuously log progress to own task
- Start L3s in planned order
- Read L3 progress logs via `slay tasks view <l3-id>`
- Poll L3s via PTY when progress stale
- Use full PTY control per L3 when needed (Shift+Tab for mode, `/compact` for context, `/effort` for reasoning, ESC to interrupt) — each L3 PTY is a full terminal
- Handle L3 escalations — resolve at L2 or escalate to L1
- Report progress + completion to L1 via PTY

**Escalation handling.**
- L3 escalates → L2 decides: in-scope (replan/reassign/fix) or escalate to L1
- L2 does NOT silently swallow unresolved escalations

**Does NOT.**
- Run git mutations
- Skip hierarchy (talk to user directly)
- Mark root task done

